        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പള്ളി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പള്ളി (paḷḷi) — both \"a church\" and \"a mosque\"; the word is older than the difference. It is also in പള്ളിക്കൂടം, \"school\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പള്ളി (paḷḷi) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil paḷḷi, Kannada paḷḷi and Telugu palli (DEDR 4018). Its first senses are \"hamlet, a public building\"; it came to name the house of worship of more than one faith. DEDR 4018 compares Sanskrit pallī̆."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One word, two buildings."
            }
          ]
        },
